===Congressional ballot===
On 6 August 1993, the National Congress convened to elect the president. Gonzalo Sánchez de Lozada was the only candidate voted on, and was supported by his MNR-MRTKL alliance as well as the UCS and [[Free Bolivia Movement|MBL]]. All others parties abstained from voting.<ref name=":0">{{cite book |last=Morales|first=Walter Q |title=A brief history of Bolivia |location=New York |publisher=Facts On File|date=2003|page=205}}</ref> Gonzalo Sánchez de Lozada was elected president while Víctor Hugo Cárdenas became Bolivia's first indigenous [[Vice President of Bolivia|vice president]].

